⬇️FULL RECIPE⬇️
265 calories 32g protein (for the entire pint, mix-ins included)

Strawberry Cheesecake Protein Ice Cream 

Original recipe from my Recipe Book
Check out the link in my bio for my Creami Recipe Book with over 150 recipes like this one!

- 1 Strawberry Protein Shake (350-400ml)
- 22g (2 tbsp) whipped (or regular) cream cheese (can sub with 1 tbsp cheesecake jello pudding mix)
- 20-25g Monk Fruit sweetener 
- A pinch of salt
- 1g (¼ tsp) xanthan gum
Mix-ins:
- 100g frozen/fresh strawberries macerated in 10-15g of sweetener + a splash of lemon juice
- ½ sheet of a graham cracker
265 cal 18g C, 8g F, 32g P

Instructions:
1. Blend all ingredients for the base and freeze (at least 16 hours)
2. At least an hour before making the ice cream, pour the strawberries into a bowl and cover with 10-15g of sweetener (if frozen, microwave them for 1 minute), stir, and place in the fridge
3. Run your pint under hot water for at least 60 seconds
4. Spin on “Lite Ice Cream” setting
5. Spin on “Respin” setting
6. Respin again if powdery
7. Make a hole down to the bottom with a butter knife (if there isn’t one already - there should already be one because we aren’t using a full pint’s worth of liquid) and fill with the strawberry topping

